cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GapFinder in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "GapFinder: AI-assisted identification of research gaps in scientific articles"
abstract: >-
  GapFinder is an open-source tool that supports researchers in identifying
  research gaps in scientific articles. It uses a retrieval-augmented generation
  (RAG) pipeline: text is extracted from PDF files, segmented, semantically
  retrieved and analysed by a large language model (Qwen 2.5-7B-Instruct or
  Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite). Each candidate gap is classified as theoretical,
  methodological, empirical or contextual, and reported with a description,
  the verbatim textual evidence from the article and a research suggestion.
  GapFinder was developed as part of doctoral research at the Federal
  University of Espírito Santo (UFES), Brazil, and operationalises the gap
  identification step of the Augmented Research Intelligence (ARI) method.
